==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Plane Cat '''at level 10.

Evolves Into '''Robocat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Tin Cat's purpose is knocking back certain Dark enemies who are difficult to repel, like [[Dark Otter]], [[Director Kurosawah|Kurosawah]], [[Le'noir]] and certain bosses. It is thus useful in stages like [[The Dom Awakens!|The Dom Awakens]] or [[Le'Grim Strikes]]. Unfortunately, common Dark enemies flinch very easily to raw damage and are often spammed, rendering its Single Attacks useless, being massively outclassed by [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] or a stack of DPS units like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg]].

His Evolved Form has a higher probability of rushing in and hitting something like Kurosawah thanks to the speed, while the true form's range and health lead to better performance against Dark Otters, the [[Dark Cyclone]] etc.

==='''Talents'''===
Robocat gains Dodge Attack, Immune to Knockback, Resist Curse, HP Buff and Attack Buff as his Talents.

HP buff and dodge attack are good for this cat's survivability, with dodge attack being especially useful, as not only does it allow for a second chance at hitting something like [[Le'Grim]] from up close, but it also allows him to sometimes block the advance of a horde of Darks for precious time. Attack up, knockback immunity and curse resistance will virtually never come into play, so ignore them.

==='''Orb'''===
There is little point in using any Orbs on this unit due to its overall lack of utility.

